<title>JAPAN: Japan May domestic WPI rises 1.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan May domestic WPI rises 1.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's domestic wholesale price index, a key component of overall WPI, rose 1.9 percent in May from a year earlier and was down 0.1 percent from the previous month, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the May WPI:</p>
<p>Year-on-year change (percent)</p>
<p>		 May	April</p>
<p> Overall     +2.7     +3.2</p>
<p> Domestic    +1.9	+1.9</p>
<p> Exports     +3.7	+5.6</p>
<p> Imports    +10.2     +13.9</p>
<p>Month-on-month change (percent, index base year 1990):</p>
<p>		 May	April	May Index</p>
<p> Overall    -0.7	 +1.7	95.1</p>
<p> Domestic   -0.1	 +1.9	97.1</p>
<p> Exports    -3.1	 +0.9	87.3</p>
<p> Imports    -3.4	 -0.1	86.8</p>
</text>
